{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q418583","formula":"AsIn","hill":"AsIn","elements":["As","In"],"composition":{"As":1.0,"In":1.0},"names":{"en":"Indium arsenide","ru":"Арсенид индия","uk":"Арсенід індію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Indium arsenide, InAs, or indium monoarsenide, is a narrow-bandgap semiconductor composed of indium and arsenic. It has the appearance of grey cubic crystals with a melting point of 942 °C. Indium arsenide is similar in properties to gallium arsenide and is a direct bandgap material, with a bandgap of 0.35 eV at room temperature. Indium arsenide is used for the construction of infrared detectors, for the wavelength range of 1.0–3.8 μm.","ru":"Арсени́д и́ндия, — бинарное неорганическое соединение индия и мышьяка. Химическая формула соединения InAs. Кристаллизуется в структуре типа сфалерита.","uk":"Арсені́д індію (InAs) — кристалічна речовина, сполука індію з арсеном. Прямозонний напівпровідник, володіє дуже малою шириною забороненої зони (0.354 еВ при 300 K)."},"fame":21,"pubchemCid":91500,"mass":189.74,"charge":0,"smiles":"[As]#[In]","inchikey":"RPQDHPTXJYYUPQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"indiganylidynearsane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-20305","atoms":18,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[6.107,0.0,0.0],[0.0,6.107,0.0],[0.0,0.0,6.107]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":4.58,"y":4.58,"z":4.58,"el":"In"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"As"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":6.107,"el":"As"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.107,"z":0.0,"el":"As"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.107,"z":6.107,"el":"As"},{"x":6.107,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"As"},{"x":6.107,"y":0.0,"z":6.107,"el":"As"},{"x":6.107,"y":6.107,"z":0.0,"el":"As"},{"x":6.107,"y":6.107,"z":6.107,"el":"As"},{"x":4.58,"y":1.527,"z":1.527,"el":"In"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.054,"z":3.054,"el":"As"},{"x":6.107,"y":3.054,"z":3.054,"el":"As"},{"x":1.527,"y":4.